<title>HONG KONG: Robinson Dept Store seeks yen funding.</title>
<headline>Robinson Dept Store seeks yen funding.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Robinson Department Store Plc has mandated Societe Generale Asia and DBS Bank to arrange a 6.8 billion yen floating rate note issue, Societe Generale Asia said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Another bank may join the arranger group.</p>
<p>The three-year notes are likely to be launched next week. Syndication will be loan style.</p>
<p>The coupon is expected to be between 120 and 135 basis points over the yen London Interbank Offered Rate.</p>
<p>Roadshows for the issue have been held in Singapore and in Hong Kong.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843-6371</p>
</text>
